WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.730
Port forwarding offers a way in which one
can use a specific port as a means to connect

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.160
to a specific device within a network.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.710
Take, for example, someone wanting to remote
into their home computer through their home

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.860
internet connection, which is a public facing
router.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.140
The problem is that the home computer probably
does not have a public IP address.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.420
However, we can use a port number to forward
the connection from the router to the PC.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.529
This is known as port forwarding and I will
open this feature on a router.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:33.130
Then, I will select Add Port Forward and then
Continue.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:42.570
I will then set my laptop as the connecting
device and enter port 3389, the Remote Desktop

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.370
port, as the port to use for this connection.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.690
Then I will select Next and the port forward
has been added.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:55.120
What is very important to do is if a port
forwarding is no longer needed, remove it,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.090
because leaving this here can risk an intruder
into this device.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:05.939
To remove this, I will select Edit, Delete
this Port Forward, and then Delete.

